<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Othman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1351</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Othman was the Marinid sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> from 1331 to 1348 and the dynasty's most ambitious ruler. He conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlemcen">Tlemcen</a> in 1337 but was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and Portugal at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rio-salado">Battle of Río Salado</a> in 1340. In 1347 he occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a>, briefly uniting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maghreb">Maghreb</a>, but Arab tribes defeated him near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a>, and his son Abu Inan took his throne; he died in 1351.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abu-al-hasan-ali-ibn-othman.jpg" alt="Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Othman" width="320" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alif · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abu_al-Hasan_ben_Uthman.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
